      "writtenOn": "2025-02-03T18:07:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You should also verify that the pca95xx wasn\u0027t already initialized.\n```\nif (!device_is_ready(PCA95XX_DEV)) {\n    device_init(PCA95XX_DEV);\n}\n```\n\nRegarding the timing, can this code check the AP power state to make sure the system is above S5?\n\nIf the system isn\u0027t in S5, then I assume we can\u0027t read the board ID - is there a sensible default that can be used in this case.  The main scenario would be if the AP issues an `EC_REBOOT_COLD_AP_OFF`.  In that case, the EC will reboot but won\u0027t automatically power up the AP.",
